 "stem": "$b$ is a middle proportional between $a={=a}$ and $c={=c}$. Find the value of $\\frac{a^2+b^2}{b^2+c^2}$ in simplest form.",
 "solution": [
  "Since $b$ is the middle proportional, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{b}{c}=m$, so $b=cm$ and $a=cm^2$.",
  "$\\frac{a^2+b^2}{b^2+c^2}=\\frac{c^2m^4+c^2m^2}{c^2m^2+c^2}=\\frac{c^2m^2(m^2+1)}{c^2(m^2+1)}=m^2$",
  "Also $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{cm^2}{c}=m^2$, so $\\frac{a^2+b^2}{b^2+c^2}=\\frac{a}{c}$.",
  "$\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{{=a}}{{=c}}=\\frac{{=p}}{{=q}}$"
 ],
 "marker": {
